<p>The U.S. Army announced the pending closure of Fort Abraham Lincoln in 1890. The fort's mission—protecting railroad survey crews and homesteaders entering Dakota Territory—had been fulfilled. The railroad reached Montana in 1881, and North and South Dakota achieved statehood in 1889. Fort Abraham Lincoln gradually declined and was abandoned in 1894.</p>

